  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nIssued 232 PM MDT SAT SEP 19 2026\nEnsemble guidance remains in good agreement regarding the \noverall pattern evolution through midweek, followed by \nincreasing spread heading into the weekend. Tuesday looks to be \na transitional day as the upper ridge axis gets pushed into the \nNorthern Rockies by an incoming Pacific trough. High \ntemperatures on Tuesday will stay mild, though slightly cooler \nthan Monday due to mid-level cloud cover and lingering \nsouthwesterly flow.\n\nGuidance has shifted toward a broader trough track further\nnorth, restricting the strongest moisture and dynamic lift\nprimarily to the Idaho panhandle and Washington. This track\nleaves our forecast area with breezy conditions and cooler\ntemperatures from Wednesday into the weekend. Thursday is\nprojected to be the warmest day of the long term as the trough\naxis and associated cold front approach, allowing valley\ntemperatures to reach the mid to upper 80s. Temperatures drop\nsharply behind the frontal passage Friday and Saturday, falling\nbelow seasonal normals. Only a small fraction of ensemble\nguidance generates measurable precipitation with the \ntrough/frontal passage next weekend, which is likely why NBM has\nno mention of precipitation in the forecast at this time.",
